    <section class="bg-ivory">
      <div class="wrap section-y">
        <div class="max-w-[68ch]">
          <Reveal>
            <p class="t-eyebrow text-ink-soft">What the ranking does not show</p>
            <h2 class="t-h2 mt-4">What actually makes a facial the best one</h2>
            <p class="t-body mt-6 leading-relaxed">
              Three variables decide whether a facial is right for your skin:
              who performs the treatment, what training that person has on your
              Fitzpatrick type and concern, and whether the treatment is
              selected at consultation or pulled from a fixed menu. None of
              the three appear in a search result. All of them show up in a
              phone call before you book.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 leading-relaxed">
              The first variable is the practitioner. A licensed esthetician
              with 7+ years treating melanin-rich skin will read a Fitzpatrick
              V face differently from a new graduate who has mostly seen
              Fitzpatrick II. Both are licensed. Both can perform a facial. The
              clinical judgment that comes from years of specific experience
              is what separates a corrective protocol from a competent
              standard one.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 leading-relaxed">
              The second is training. The advanced modalities offered in San
              Diego — DMK Enzyme Therapy, Procell microchanneling,
              medical-grade peels — require specific training that not every
              esthetician holds. A studio offering a corrective protocol
              without the training to back it up is offering a different
              service than it appears to be offering.
            </p>
            <p class="t-body mt-5 leading-relaxed">
              The third is whether the treatment is selected at consultation or
              run from a fixed protocol. A studio that performs the same
              facial every visit, with the same steps, regardless of what the
              skin shows, is running a relaxation service under a corrective
              label. A studio that varies the protocol based on what the skin
              is doing that day is running a corrective service.
            </p>
